ust  no room for it in society ever and  everyone's just trying to be a better  version of themself and there's just you  know it's just I think if people and  fans and young fans see me react in a  powerful way to people body shaming or  just being negative I feel like that  will I don't know maybe trickle down and  inspire them to stand up to like the  school bully or to whoever whomever is  you know they're they're facing  adversity with so yeah I I sometimes  respond and my own way to those idiots  and you seem to be embracing that role  of being a role model which i think is  really great and it's also gives your  fans someone to look up to what does  that mean to you to have that position  as a role model well I think being a  role model is sort of a byproduct of  just being yourself and I think my fans  really gravitate to that and I think  that I I try not to put too much  pressure on it because the whole reason  I think a lot of them have been inspired  by me whether it's my music or the way  that I sort of perceived on social media  or interviews is that I  I'm just myself and I feel like they  they want to be like that too they want  to be themselves and so if that's like  what has made me a role model I think  that I can continue doing that without  any pressure because I'm just being  meirin and I don't really think I could  be anyone else so I kind of take it as  an honor but also not a heavy crown to  wear yeah  now those fans have been following your  success for years now you've had so much  up to this point but this has been a  real banner year for you  you know you've been able to reach out  to a whole new audience with your  collaboration was that have you felt the  difference yeah I mean I don't know how  it lined up this way but doing the song  with Zedd with the middle and then being  on this tour with nyle which is a pop  tour which I haven't really done yeah  it's been a crazy year simultaneously  with my own country stuff still  happening and I'm on my last single for  my debut album right now rich and yeah  so to sort of weave in this pop world  throughout my year has been really cool  it's like a new challenge for me and I  think it's opened up a lot of pop fans  and international fans to my music but  also the world of country music which is  very cool yeah it's been so fun to be a  part of both of those things it seems to  be going both ways and there's there's a  lot of crossover now do you think that  that that sort of will break down the  barriers of how people think about music  like country fans just being country  fans and pop fans not really considering  country music but you're breaking that  barrier down essentially well thanks I  would hope it breaks barriers down  because I I say this in a lot of my  shows because my album isn't just one  thing it's not just country it's not pop  it's not just R&amp;B or bluegrass I mean  it's just a bunch of different stuff  because that's how I was raised  and I think most of us listen to more  than one genre of music I mean if you  only listen or order one thing off the  menu each day you're going to get  you know tired of it I want to open  people up to not being ashamed to love  everything and I think honestly with  streaming services it's broken a lot of  those boundaries down just organically  because people can just bounce to  different playlists genre to genre and  it's just about good music it's not  about the genre yeah
 

